# Symbolic shapes: the order is chosen only if it is provably no more expensive
# for every N (arrays are never empty). Here `A @ (B @ v)` is 4·N² against
# 2·N³ + 2·N², so it wins for every N. The second chain compares N·N·M against
# N·M·K, which depends on N, M and K: it is left as written.
A: Matrix[N, N]
B: Matrix[N, N]
v: Vector[N]
x = A @ B @ v
P: Matrix[N, M]
Q: Matrix[M, K]
R: Matrix[K, K]
y = A @ P @ Q
print(x, y)
